Q.1	Write a Java Program to implement I/O Decorator for converting uppercase letters to lower case letters.      [15M].

Solution: - 

ToLower.java

public interface ToLower {
    public void lower(String ch);
}

LowerCase.java

public class LowerCase implements ToLower {

    public void lower(String ch) {
        ch = ch.toLowerCase();
        System.out.println("Lowercase: " + ch);
    }
}

Decorator.java

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Decorator {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        ToLower lo = new LowerCase();

        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter String: ");
        String s = sc.nextLine();

        lo.lower(s);

        sc.close();
    }
}
2. Write a Java Program to implement Singleton pattern for multithreading.

class Singleton {

    private static Singleton obj;

    private Singleton() {
        System.out.println("Singleton Object Created");
    }

    public static synchronized Singleton getInstance() {

        if (obj == null) {
            obj = new Singleton();
        }

        return obj;
    }
}

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Thread t1 = new Thread(() -> {
            Singleton s = Singleton.getInstance();
            System.out.println("Thread 1: " + s);
        });

        Thread t2 = new Thread(() -> {
            Singleton s = Singleton.getInstance();
            System.out.println("Thread 2: " + s);
        });

        t1.start();
        t2.start();
    }
}

